    "reasoning": "All four current answers agree with the earlier answers and each question's own captured worked solution. The extreme value theorem applies to continuous real-valued functions on closed bounded intervals. q-73484: I includes negative cosine values, where the square root is undefined; II is not closed; III is closed and the function is continuous there. q-73481: I includes negative inputs, where the real fourth root is undefined; II and III lie in the domain and the denominator x²+1 never vanishes. q-73495: I contains a jump at zero, with left limit −1 and right limit 1; II has a continuous exponential function; III is not closed. q-131066: I contains a jump at zero, with left limit 2 and right limit 0; II contains only continuous tangent values; III contains π/2, where tangent is undefined. No grades were supplied; confirmation is based on the captured worked solutions.",
